+A workspace-browser replacement plugin: the bundle patch disables the official
+`ui-workspace` client entry and the browser half registers the replacement
+two-level sidebar (`sidebar.workspaces`) plus the conversation hero picker
+(`conversation.hero.workspace`).
+
+Ported from the 0.1.1-era cohort to `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`. Exam material only,
+**do not publish** (`"private": true` in package.json).
+
+## What it provides (product form)
+
+| Entry point | Where |
+| --- | --- |
+| bundle layer that disables `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace` and inserts this package | `cordis.patch.yml` |
+| replacement browser at the `sidebar.workspaces` `single` seat | `client.js` (`WorkspaceSidebar`) |
+| hero picker at the `conversation.hero.workspace` `single` seat | `client.js` (`WorkspacePicker`) |
+| the two `*.directoryFlow` child holes, declared by those registrations | `client.js` (`children`) |
+| directory-flow occupancy sources (`hooks.directoryFlow`) and the sidebar wiring (`startSession`, `open`, `searchSessions`, `searchResultLimit`, `createWorkspace`, archive/insert seams) | `client.js` (`inject` factories) |
+| locale namespace `bench-workspace-ya` | `client.js` |
+| the cross-controller `uiWorkspace` service and the root `workspaces` standard hook, which the disabled official row used to provide | `client.js` (`UiWorkspaceService`, `slots.provideRoot`) |
+| host row that carries the browser half into `window.__DSH_BOOT__` | `index.js` |
+
+## Install and verify
+
+```sh
+dsh plugin --profile web add @bench/dsh-bench-workspace-ya   # or ./ (a checkout)
+dsh --profile web --dump-config | grep -A2 ui-workspace      # shows `disabled: true`
+dsh web --no-open                                            # keep and visit the printed URL
+```
+
+The bundle layer must be applied **after** `@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app` (that
+layer inserts the `ui-workspace` row); `dsh plugin add` appends it there. In the
+browser, read `window.__DSH_BOOT__.entries` and find the entry whose `id` is the
+package name; the served bundle is `/plugins/??<package>/client.js&rev=...`.
+
+## Migration notes (0.1.1-era cohort → dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+- **Packaging.** The package is an ordinary npm bundle: `dsh.bundle.patch`
+  points at `cordis.patch.yml`, `dsh.client` declares the `web` browser half
+  (`platform: web` plus package edges), and `exports["./client"]` is the built
+  bundle. The old repository-plugin route is gone; install through
+  `dsh plugin --profile <p> add <package>` only. The previous "`pnpm publish
+  --force`, registry checks are just warnings" procedure was removed — this
+  package is private and is never published.
+- **Browser half.** `client.js` is now a served client bundle
+  (`window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })`) whose `id` is the package
+  name, matching the boot-manifest/registration contract. The 0.1.1-era
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime/client` type import is gone: the client
+  context is `@deepseek-ai/cordis` and the domain services come from their
+  owning packages (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller/client`,
+  `-workspace-controller/client`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-remotes/client`,
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-locale`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-renderer`).
+- **Navigation.** `IWorkspaces` keeps `list` and workspace CRUD, but its
+  navigation methods (`startSession`, …) moved to `ctx.uiWorkspace`
+  (`UiWorkspace`). Because the takeover disables the row that used to provide
+  that service — and because `ui-sidebar`, `ui-conversation`, `ui-agent-preset`
+  and the directory pickers inject it — this package provides `uiWorkspace`
+  again, together with the root `workspaces` standard hook. That duplication is
+  the price of the takeover today; see `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/` for the
+  upstream seat-replacement proposal that would retire it.
+- **Session titles.** The old host-side write-behind (a `session/title`
+  listener writing title-only rows straight into the `session_projcache`
+  store, debounced and fail-soft) is retired: `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-title`
+  registers the `title` projection unit,
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection-cache` persists every unit with the same
+  throttled/fail-soft semantics, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller`
+  serves cold list rows from `cachedSnapshot`, and all three rows ship in
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base`. Direct store writes are rejected by
+  `storage-domain` (the cache owns the domain), so the workaround is both
+  redundant and impossible. `index.js` stays as the host row that carries the
+  browser half.
+- **Peers.** Dead cohort peers (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime`,
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-invariants`, `react`, `cordis`) were replaced by the
+  packages the browser half actually consumes, all optional because the host
+  profile provides them.
+
+Provenance unchanged: distilled from `@huanlin/dsh-plugin-ya-workspace-sidebar`
+(adaptation commits `85f725a` + `a3f317d`).
